# SEO Checklist

Every page change should be checked against this list.

## Required on every page

```tsx
import { Meta } from '../ui/base/Meta';

// Minimum:
<Meta
  title="Page Title — Fellowship Event Hall"   // < 60 chars
  description="140–160 char description..."    // target 140–160 chars
  jsonLd={/* schema from src/utils/StructuredData.ts */}
/>
```

- Title < 60 characters, includes primary keyword
- Description 140–160 characters, ends with benefit or soft CTA
- `jsonLd` always provided — never skip structured data

## Structured data by page

| Page | Required schemas |
|---|---|
| `index.tsx` | `localBusinessJsonLd()`, `eventVenueJsonLd()`, `offerCatalogJsonLd(...)` |
| `packages.tsx` | `offerCatalogJsonLd(...)`, `breadcrumbJsonLd(...)` |
| `gallery.tsx` | `breadcrumbJsonLd(...)` |
| New page | At minimum `breadcrumbJsonLd(...)` |

Import helpers from `src/utils/StructuredData.ts`. Do not write raw JSON-LD objects inline.

## Heading hierarchy

- Exactly one `<h1>` per page
- `<h2>` for major sections, `<h3>` for sub-sections
- Never skip levels (no jumping from `<h1>` to `<h3>`)

## Images

- Every `<img>` and `<Image>` (next/image) must have non-empty `alt`
- Decorative images: `alt=""`
- Hero/feature images: describe what is shown, include location keyword where natural ("Event hall dining room setup for wedding, Dacula GA")

## Open Graph

`Meta.tsx` wires OG title/description/image automatically. For pages with a unique hero image, pass it through `next-seo`'s `openGraph.images` prop.

## Site-wide copy

All canonical site data lives in `src/utils/AppConfig.ts`:
- `AppConfig.url` — canonical base URL
- `AppConfig.title`, `AppConfig.description` — global fallbacks
- `AppConfig.address`, `AppConfig.telephone`, `AppConfig.email` — used in structured data

Never hardcode the domain or contact info anywhere else.

## Sitemap

`postbuild` runs `next-sitemap` automatically. Do not suppress it. New pages are included automatically. If a page should be excluded (e.g., a thank-you page), add it to `next-sitemap.config.js`.
